<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson jumps after Nokia report.</title>
<headline>Ericsson jumps after Nokia report.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecommunications company L.M. Ericsson's share jumped 10 crowns to 247.5 crowns after rival Nokia posted strong first quarter earnings.</p>
<p>Brokers said the share was also strengthened by an analyst's comment that the share price should be around 300 crowns. Nokia said a strong upturn in handset sales helped first quarter profit surge by 260 percent to 1.45 billion markka from 399 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
